# Validation, auth, security

Express service under `src/` only. This service validates with Joi, not Zod.

## Validation

Schemas live in `validations/*.validation.js` and run through `validate(schema)` in `middlewares/validate.js`. Reuse `objectId`, `mobile`, and `password` from `custom.validation.js`. Validate `params`, `query`, and `body` as each route needs them.

```javascript
const getUser = {
  params: Joi.object().keys({
    userId: Joi.string().custom(objectId),
  }),
};
```

Do not validate ad hoc inside the controller (`if (!req.body.email.includes('@'))`). Do not use `req.params.userId` in a query unless the route has `objectId` validation.

## Auth

Passport JWT is configured in `config/passport.js`. Protect a route with `auth()` or `auth('right-name')`. Rights still come from `req.accessList`. Only the gateway may set `x-access-list`. Strip that header when the caller is not the gateway. Read the JWT secret from `config.jwt.secret`. Never hardcode it. Hash passwords with bcrypt in model hooks. Never log or return a password.

## Middleware order in `app.js`

1. morgan, except in test
2. helmet
3. express.json and urlencoded
4. xss, then mongoSanitize
5. compression
6. custom headers (`x-user-id`, `x-access-list`, and the rest)
7. CORS allowlist
8. passport.initialize and the jwt strategy
9. `/v1` routes
10. 404, then errorConverter, then errorHandler

Security middleware stays before `/v1`. Do not mount it after the routes.

## Rules

| Do | Don't |
|---|---|
| CORS allowlist from `app.js` | `origin: '*'` on the production API |
| Joi on every input | Trust `req.body` inside a query |
| `pick` an allowlist | Merge all of `req.body` into config |
| Private S3 plus type and size checks | Public uploads, or trusting Content-Type alone |
| Winston for app logs | Log tokens, passwords, or full bodies |

`middlewares/rateLimiter.js` exists. Enable it on `/v1/auth` in production.
